00:07:46.770 --> 00:07:49.120
and then decide which chart
type you want to pick.

00:07:49.120 --> 00:07:50.520
And indeed, the likely several ways

00:07:50.520 --> 00:07:52.190
of how to visualize this one example here

00:07:52.190 --> 00:07:54.250
would be these bubble charts.

00:07:54.250 --> 00:07:56.030
So, I'd say bubble charts are always great

00:07:56.030 --> 00:07:57.810
when you have three number dimensions

00:07:57.810 --> 00:07:59.630
that you wanna have in one chart.

00:07:59.630 --> 00:08:01.810
So, here the X-axis
has the marketing spend

00:08:01.810 --> 00:08:03.690
on the Y-axis, the unit price.

00:08:03.690 --> 00:08:05.740
And I think you can very
well see the correlation.

00:08:05.740 --> 00:08:07.840
You could now also insert a trend line

00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:10.430
if you would want to really
make that more salient.

00:08:10.430 --> 00:08:13.300
But then also you see in
the size of the bubbles

00:08:13.300 --> 00:08:17.110
that the areas of these bubbles
represent the volume sold.

00:08:17.110 --> 00:08:18.470
And the other thing
that's also pretty clear

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:20.710
