00:10:38.220 --> 00:10:40.500
And surely, it's a great
idea to be prepared.

00:10:40.500 --> 00:10:42.860
So, with all of this in mind,
let's look at a third example

00:10:42.860 --> 00:10:44.540
of choosing the right chart type.

00:10:44.540 --> 00:10:46.320
So, here you have the example of an P&amp;L.

00:10:46.320 --> 00:10:48.790
So, profit and loss
statement of a company.

00:10:48.790 --> 00:10:51.320
One of the three key financial statements

00:10:51.320 --> 00:10:52.600
that companies need to produce.

00:10:52.600 --> 00:10:55.010
So, let's imagine you
would want to visualize

00:10:55.010 --> 00:10:59.030
this P&amp;L in the chart, which
one would you like to choose?

00:10:59.030 --> 00:11:01.250
And here again, pause a
moment, think about this.

00:11:01.250 --> 00:11:03.220
Maybe this is less proven, less clear.

00:11:03.220 --> 00:11:06.140
Because indeed, one chart
type that is extensively used

00:11:06.140 --> 00:11:08.120
in consulting that is very well suited

00:11:08.120 --> 00:11:12.250
also to visualize things like
P&amp;Ls are the waterfall charts.

00:11:12.250 --> 00:11:13.083
So, what we have here

00:11:13.083 --> 00:11:14.850
is the data entry window of think-cell.

00:11:14.850 --> 00:11:17.090
You can see that I already
copied in all the numbers.

00:11:17.090 --> 00:11:18.830
The letter E stands for equals.

00:11:18.830 --> 00:11:20.150
So, think-cell here can help you

00:11:20.150 --> 00:11:21.173
to automatically calculate
totals and subtotals.

00:11:23.100 --> 00:11:25.280
So, no need to do this manually anymore.

00:11:25.280 --> 00:11:27.250
Think-cell will do the
calculations for you

00:11:27.250 --> 00:11:29.430
and provide you with the correct results.

00:11:29.430 --> 00:11:31.840
And also, notice how you
can stack waterfall segments

00:11:31.840 --> 00:11:34.200
just by writing the
numbers under each other

00:11:34.200 --> 00:11:36.180
here in the column for the personal cost.

00:11:36.180 --> 00:11:37.810
And indeed, this is the result.

00:11:37.810 --> 00:11:40.310
This is what the waterfall
chart will look like.

00:11:40.310 --> 00:11:41.850
But now you're already seeing a problem,

00:11:41.850 --> 00:11:44.330
and this is because all
the numbers are entered

00:11:44.330 --> 00:11:45.530
in million, right?

00:11:45.530 --> 00:11:47.030
So, the numbers are quite long.

00:11:47.030 --> 00:11:49.800
This is surely not how you
would want them to look like.

00:11:49.800 --> 00:11:50.680
So, what do you do now?

00:11:50.680 --> 00:11:53.080
Do you need to now go back
to the data entry mask

00:11:53.080 --> 00:11:55.250
and change all the numbers or the Excel?

00:11:55.250 --> 00:11:57.428
By the way, you can also
integrate things in Excel

00:11:57.428 --> 00:11:59.830
to automatically update charts like this.

00:11:59.830 --> 00:12:00.690
Well, of course not.

00:12:00.690 --> 00:12:02.520
Because one of the many very handy

00:12:02.520 --> 00:12:03.710
think-cell functionalities

00:12:03.710 --> 00:12:05.910
is that just with a couple of clicks,

00:12:05.910 --> 00:12:08.440
you can really transpose
all these numbers.

00:12:08.440 --> 00:12:09.273
And for instance,

00:12:09.273 --> 00:12:12.090
round them to millions
as I'm doing right here.

00:12:12.090 --> 00:12:13.630
And just with a couple of clicks,

00:12:13.630 --> 00:12:14.730
you have already the chart now

00:12:14.730 --> 00:12:16.800
exactly the way that you want it to look.

00:12:16.800 --> 00:12:18.130
So, now last but not least,

00:12:18.130 --> 00:12:19.980
let's look at some typical errors

00:12:19.980 --> 00:12:22.100
that people do when they create charts.

00:12:22.100 --> 00:12:23.750
And I think one of the main problems

00:12:23.750 --> 00:12:26.790
is if you just use the
built-in PowerPoint charts,

00:12:26.790 --> 00:12:28.560
so not use the think-cell charts,

00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:30.840
then often these charts come already

00:12:30.840 --> 00:12:33.350
pre-configured with some problems.

00:12:33.350 --> 00:12:35.130
So, all the charts you see right here

00:12:35.130 --> 00:12:37.340
are design templates that also suggest

00:12:37.340 --> 00:12:40.550
that layouts suggest that
designs within PowerPoint.

00:12:40.550 --> 00:12:43.110
So, here you see charts
with these glossy effects,

00:12:43.110 --> 00:12:45.750
with shadows, with 3D effects,

00:12:45.750 --> 00:12:47.970
with these rear shaded backgrounds.

00:12:47.970 --> 00:12:49.950
Now, we could look into
this in much more detail

00:12:49.950 --> 00:12:53.000
but I hope that you agree just
at the first look and feel

00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:55.500
that these charts don't
really look professional.

00:12:55.500 --> 00:12:58.300
So, let's just look here at
this profitability surface chart

00:12:58.300 --> 00:13:01.730
which again is one of the
suggested templates by PowerPoint.

00:13:01.730 --> 00:13:02.600
How this looks.

00:13:02.600 --> 00:13:05.970
I mean, it's virtually impossible
to get really any insight,

00:13:05.970 --> 00:13:08.200
any message out of this chart at all.

00:13:08.200 --> 00:13:10.560
Just to distill any
number out of it at all.

00:13:10.560 --> 00:13:13.090
So, you should really avoid
all layouts like this.

00:13:13.090 --> 00:13:15.740
I think we now extensively
already talked about formatting.

00:13:15.740 --> 00:13:17.690
I wanna leave you with
one last piece of advice,

00:13:17.690 --> 00:13:18.710
because this is something

00:13:18.710 --> 00:13:20.720
that I often also see done wrongly.

00:13:20.720 --> 00:13:23.210
And this is a general trying to avoid.

00:13:23.210 --> 00:13:24.820
Having too many different charts,

00:13:24.820 --> 00:13:27.670
too many different messages on one slide.

00:13:27.670 --> 00:13:29.590
There's the basic rule of thumb

00:13:29.590 --> 00:13:32.690
which says one message per slide.

00:13:32.690 --> 00:13:35.890
Really try to stick to
one message per slide.

00:13:35.890 --> 00:13:38.910
This usually makes the whole
storytelling much easier,

00:13:38.910 --> 00:13:41.040
helps you to create more to the point,

00:13:41.040 --> 00:13:43.640
nicely formatted, nicely layout pages.

00:13:43.640 --> 00:13:45.940
Several charts on one page can be okay

00:13:45.940 --> 00:13:48.480
but only if you really
need all these charts

00:13:48.480 --> 00:13:51.223
next to each other to really
get the one message out

00:13:51.223 --> 00:13:52.720
that you want to share.

00:13:52.720 --> 00:13:54.500
Otherwise, rather split it up

00:13:54.500 --> 00:13:56.210
and show them on different pages.

